# G127 — Signature Maker

*v2. See `signature-maker.md` for prose: per-point pressure + timestamp,
Catmull-Rom splines integer-scaled, endpoint-preserving smoothing,
variable-width disk-stamp render, bounding-box normalization.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Signature Capture

[signature-capture @save-path
    IN ORDER TO
        capture an ink signature from pen input with pressure and timing
        smooth the stroke with endpoint preservation
        normalize to a unit coordinate system for later comparison
        render to a variable-width raster and save to the vault

    @sig <- [sig[new-signature]]

    until @save-pressed [
        sync @pen-down
            @stroke <- [sig[start-stroke]]

        sync @pen-move (@x @y @pressure @t)
            [sig[add-point {stroke: @stroke,
                             x: @x, y: @y,
                             pressure: @pressure, t-ms: @t}]]

        sync @pen-up
            @smoothed <- [sig[smooth-stroke {stroke: @stroke, steps: 8}]]
            [sig[add-stroke {signature: @sig, stroke: @smoothed}]]
    ]

    @normalized <- [sig[normalize {signature: @sig,
                                     target-w: 1000, target-h: 1000}]]
    @img <- [sig[render {signature: @normalized,
                          width: 500, height: 200,
                          max-width: 6,
                          bg: white, ink: black}]]
    [vault[save {path: @save-path, image: @img}]]
]

---

## Choreographic Case: Signature Verification

[signature-verify @proposed @reference @threshold
    IN ORDER TO
        decide whether @proposed matches @reference
        by comparing normalized point-sets within @threshold distance

    @norm-p <- [sig[normalize {signature: @proposed,
                                 target-w: 1000, target-h: 1000}]]
    @norm-r <- [sig[normalize {signature: @reference,
                                 target-w: 1000, target-h: 1000}]]
    @distance <- [sig[similarity-distance {a: @norm-p, b: @norm-r}]]

    @distance
        where value at most @threshold
        -> #verified true
        || -> #verified false
]

---

## Verb Surface

[sig
    new-signature
    start-stroke
    add-point          {stroke, x, y, pressure, t-ms}
    add-stroke         {signature, stroke}
    point-count        {signature}
    bounding-box       {signature}
    catmull-rom        {p0, p1, p2, p3, t}
    smooth-stroke      {stroke, steps}
    normalize          {signature, target-w, target-h}
    similarity-distance {a, b}
    render             {signature, width, height, max-width, bg, ink}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: normalize-then-compare as required composition

[sig[similarity-distance {a: @raw-a, b: @raw-b}
    where both signatures are first normalized to the same target box
        otherwise the distance is dominated by size difference
        and tells you nothing about shape similarity
]

Enforcing the precondition in the `where` clause means the resolver
can refuse un-normalized inputs with resistance pointing to the fix.

---

## Integer-scaled Catmull-Rom as cross-resolver contract

[sig[catmull-rom {p0: @p0, p1: @p1, p2: @p2, p3: @p3, t: @t}
    where
        t is 0..=1000 (integer-scaled fraction)
        and the curve passes through p1 at t=0 and p2 at t=1000
        and all arithmetic is integer (scaled by powers of 1000)
        and final division by 2,000,000
        and result is byte-identical across all conforming resolvers
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @s <- [sig[new-signature]]
    [sig[add-stroke {signature: @s,
                       stroke: {points: [{x: 10, y: 20, pressure: 512, t-ms: 0}
                                          {x: 30, y: 40, pressure: 768, t-ms: 100}
                                          {x: 50, y: 30, pressure: 1024, t-ms: 200}
                                          {x: 70, y: 50, pressure: 512, t-ms: 300}]}}]]

    -> [sig[point-count {signature: @s}]]       ;; -> 4
    -> [sig[bounding-box {signature: @s}]]       ;; -> (10, 20, 70, 50)

    -> [sig[catmull-rom
             {p0: (0, 0), p1: (10, 10), p2: (20, 10), p3: (30, 0),
              t: 500}]]
    ;; -> some interpolated midpoint, byte-identical across resolvers

    @norm <- [sig[normalize {signature: @s, target-w: 1000, target-h: 1000}]]
    -> [sig[bounding-box {signature: @norm}]]    ;; -> (0, 0, 999, 999)

    -> [sig[similarity-distance {a: @s, b: @s}]]  ;; -> 0 (self-similarity)
]
